This paper investigates the normalized ground state solutions for the given biharmonic Choquard type equation \begin{align*}
  \begin{split}
  \left\{
  \begin{array}{ll}
  \Delta^2u-\beta\Delta u=\lambda u+\left(\frac{1}{|x|^\mu}*F(u)\right)f(u), & x\in\mathbb{R}^4, \\
  \int_{\mathbb{R}^4}u^2dx=c^2, &
  \end{array}
  \right.
  \end{split}
  \end{align*} under specific conditions on the parameters $\beta$, $\lambda$, and $\mu$. By employing a change of variables and applying the concentration compactness principle along with a linking argument, we establish the existence of a normalized ground state solution for this equation.
